WEBVTT

00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:01.730
"One day in September"

00:00:01.730 --> 00:00:02.940
"School District 7, Bridge 3"

00:00:22.830 --> 00:00:26.830
Patient in transport is Hitokawa Hasami,
16-year-old female.

00:00:26.830 --> 00:00:30.300
Fell from Bridge 3 in
School District 7 into the river.

00:00:30.300 --> 00:00:30.710
--We found what appears to be
a suicide note in her pocket.

00:00:30.710 --> 00:00:32.970
--H-Huh? I'm still alive...
--We found what appears to be
a suicide note in her pocket.

00:00:32.970 --> 00:00:35.760
--H-Huh? I'm still alive...
--Heart and lungs have stopped;
currently attempting resuscitation.

00:00:35.760 --> 00:00:39.260
Aww, I can't even die right.

00:00:39.260 --> 00:00:42.890
Damn. I'm a failure at everything I do.

00:00:42.890 --> 00:00:44.940
She appears to have regained consciousness.

00:00:44.940 --> 00:00:48.310
That explains it. She's 
a Level 2 pyrokinesist.

00:00:48.310 --> 00:00:51.780
Not a half-bad subject.
Her ability is suited for combat.

00:00:51.780 --> 00:00:55.280
Best of all, she's an "evil" criminal
who's guilty of suicide.

00:00:55.280 --> 00:00:56.860
Huh?

00:00:56.860 --> 00:01:00.780
Good. Let's go ahead and dispose of her.

00:01:00.780 --> 00:01:04.120
Acknowledged. So then, following
Hitokawa Hasami's plunge into the river,

00:01:04.120 --> 00:01:09.040
attempts to resuscitate her
proved ineffective, and she drowned.

00:01:09.040 --> 00:01:13.210
Are you sure about the liquid?
They won't figure it out at the autopsy?

00:01:13.210 --> 00:01:15.970
We're making sure to
use water from the river.

00:01:22.680 --> 00:01:29.190
Rest easy. We will use your body
to serve the cause of justice.

00:01:29.190 --> 00:01:33.030
--By DA's dogma.
--By DA's dogma.

00:01:33.030 --> 00:01:35.280
By DA's dogma.

00:01:53.500 --> 00:01:59.510
"A Certain Scientific Accelerator"

00:03:07.370 --> 00:03:08.910
"Three days later"

00:03:09.000 --> 00:03:14.130
"#02 Necromancer (Raiser of the Dead)"

00:03:13.420 --> 00:03:15.040
Nobody told me!

00:03:15.040 --> 00:03:17.800
Imagine, reanimating even dog corpses!

00:03:21.090 --> 00:03:22.720
Here.

00:03:22.720 --> 00:03:28.310
Antibiotics. Once the infection takes hold,
it'll be too late. Inject yourself.

00:03:28.310 --> 00:03:31.390
HQ calling Alpha. Report your status.

00:03:31.390 --> 00:03:34.270
This is Alpha. One injured.

00:03:34.270 --> 00:03:36.940
Bravo is currently pursuing target.

00:03:36.940 --> 00:03:39.230
We've pinpointed the
facility that she broke into,

00:03:39.230 --> 00:03:41.860
but said facility has
been designated off-limits.

00:03:41.860 --> 00:03:46.410
In that area, if you're talking off-limits,
you must mean the hospital.

00:03:46.410 --> 00:03:50.700
Request confirmation of our next action.
Proceed or withdraw?

00:03:50.700 --> 00:03:53.670
If we're proceeding,
will we need revised procedures?

00:03:53.670 --> 00:03:55.920
No need. Carry out your mission.

00:03:55.920 --> 00:03:58.960
Just make sure not to bring any harm
to the patients in the hospital.

00:03:58.960 --> 00:04:01.760
Yeah, be sure you're careful.

00:04:01.760 --> 00:04:03.430
The target you're after

00:04:03.430 --> 00:04:07.550
is a unique esper who can control
the corpses of dead creatures.

00:04:04.220 --> 00:04:05.930
"Morgue"

00:04:07.550 --> 00:04:10.930
Underestimate her,
and the damage will only increase.

00:04:10.930 --> 00:04:12.310
Copy that.

00:04:14.270 --> 00:04:15.900
Not here.

00:04:15.900 --> 00:04:20.190
To reiterate, once you locate the target,
secure them immediately.

00:04:20.190 --> 00:04:23.650
In doing so, do not bring any harm
to the patients in the hospital.

00:04:23.650 --> 00:04:24.910
--Roger.
--Roger.

00:05:10.830 --> 00:05:12.450
Why, you!

00:05:24.300 --> 00:05:29.600
Target spotted! Near the second floor
west staircase, fleeing east!

00:05:40.310 --> 00:05:42.230
Not what I have written here.

00:05:44.110 --> 00:05:47.860
This is an emergency. Please listen to me.

00:05:47.860 --> 00:05:49.620
Where is this girl?

00:06:12.510 --> 00:06:14.810
Her life...

00:06:18.770 --> 00:06:24.190
Antiskill. We've caught a criminal
that snuck into the hospital.

00:06:24.190 --> 00:06:27.570
We appreciate your cooperation.

00:06:27.570 --> 00:06:32.910
Hmph, he's feigning indifference
to avoid any trouble.

00:06:42.840 --> 00:06:44.710
Huh?

00:06:49.090 --> 00:06:50.840
You apprehended her?

00:06:50.840 --> 00:06:52.800
Of course.

00:06:52.800 --> 00:06:57.100
HQ, HQ, this is Alpha. Target secured.

00:06:57.100 --> 00:07:00.890
Encountered patient inside the hospital
in the process, but avoided contact.

00:07:00.890 --> 00:07:03.610
This is HQ. Good work.

00:07:03.610 --> 00:07:07.860
Mm-hmm, so it sounds like
you didn't have to use the "coffin."

00:07:07.860 --> 00:07:10.280
You must be the guest. No, we didn't.

00:07:10.280 --> 00:07:13.780
Good. They're still difficult to control,

00:07:13.780 --> 00:07:16.330
so I was hoping you wouldn't
have to use them, if possible.

00:07:16.330 --> 00:07:19.750
If things went wrong,
you all would have been killed, too.

00:07:19.750 --> 00:07:21.500
We wouldn't screw up like that.

00:07:21.500 --> 00:07:25.420
Are you sure? Well, Esther has been secured,

00:07:25.420 --> 00:07:28.800
and after a little research,
the coffins' performance will improve.

00:07:28.800 --> 00:07:32.760
Mm-hmm, I think they'll be
weapons that even you can use.

00:07:32.760 --> 00:07:37.930
Tch, some punk kid who's never been
in the field. We're pulling out.

00:07:40.180 --> 00:07:42.940
You really did a number on us earlier.

00:07:42.940 --> 00:07:48.280
Ordinarily, I'd see that you got some
significant payback, but I won't kill you.

00:07:48.280 --> 00:07:50.740
You can still be of use 
to justice, after all.

00:07:53.450 --> 00:07:57.660
We were told not to kill you,
but if we want to correct a foolish child,

00:07:57.660 --> 00:08:00.830
we <i>do</i> need to administer
some kind of punishment, don't we?

00:08:05.460 --> 00:08:09.630
Don't overdo it. This isn't like last time.

00:08:14.550 --> 00:08:16.010
We're moving out.

00:08:16.010 --> 00:08:17.350
Copy.

00:08:19.970 --> 00:08:21.390
What?

00:08:21.390 --> 00:08:22.560
What is it?

00:08:22.560 --> 00:08:25.020
Somebody's blocking our way.

00:08:25.020 --> 00:08:26.230
Hey, move it!

00:08:26.230 --> 00:08:28.860
Is the girl inside there?

00:08:30.530 --> 00:08:32.280
You're the one from earlier.

00:08:32.490 --> 00:08:36.740
There's something I wanna ask her.
Leave her here.

00:08:37.320 --> 00:08:39.550
The girl in our custody is a criminal.

00:08:40.080 --> 00:08:42.580
This is no business of
a civilian such as yourself.

00:08:43.080 --> 00:08:45.330
Hurry on back to your bed in the hospital.

00:08:45.580 --> 00:08:49.340
You guys aren't Antiskill, are you?

00:08:49.800 --> 00:08:53.720
What are you talking about?
We keep the peace in this city--

00:08:53.720 --> 00:08:57.510
Those guys are so damn 
serious it's laughable.

00:08:57.510 --> 00:09:01.350
They would never suddenly aim
their guns at an unarmed civilian.

00:09:03.600 --> 00:09:08.610
Hmph. Antiskill? Those guys are fakes.

00:09:08.980 --> 00:09:11.320
We, the members of DA, are the real justice!

00:09:11.440 --> 00:09:15.950
We are Academy City's 
hunting dogs of justice,

00:09:15.950 --> 00:09:19.780
and with our fangs, we flush out evil,
chew it up, and destroy it!

00:09:20.030 --> 00:09:21.160
DA?

00:09:21.450 --> 00:09:24.910
Move! Or do you want to be
chewed up by the fangs of justice?!

00:09:25.210 --> 00:09:27.080
Go ahead and try.

00:09:27.120 --> 00:09:28.000
What?

00:09:28.000 --> 00:09:31.580
Don't. Our orders are
to do no harm to the patients.

00:09:32.710 --> 00:09:36.050
Patients? Where do you see any patients?

00:09:36.050 --> 00:09:40.300
This guy, who stands in the
way of our justice, is just vermin.

00:09:40.300 --> 00:09:43.680
And I exterminate vermin
with the fangs of justice!

00:09:44.180 --> 00:09:45.980
By DA's dogma.

00:09:47.810 --> 00:09:49.440
By DA's dogma.

00:09:50.560 --> 00:09:52.520
By DA's dogma.

00:09:52.690 --> 00:09:55.900
This is your last warning. Get lost, vermin!

00:10:04.540 --> 00:10:08.350
Justice? Is that all you've got?

00:10:08.960 --> 00:10:10.630
You're an esper?

00:10:11.170 --> 00:10:12.750
The hell with it! Run him over!

00:10:12.750 --> 00:10:13.420
Roger.

00:10:13.880 --> 00:10:16.470
Don't get too full of yourself, vermin!

00:10:16.470 --> 00:10:21.390
Disciplining monster children
like yourself is part of our mission!

00:10:34.570 --> 00:10:35.670
Hey!

00:10:36.030 --> 00:10:39.700
Beat it, while I'm still only
handing out gentle love taps.

00:10:39.700 --> 00:10:41.490
Otherwise, I'll crush you!

00:10:41.780 --> 00:10:46.350
Y-You little... We don't put up with vermin!

00:10:47.120 --> 00:10:51.500
Let me show you what
absolute justice looks like!

00:10:58.760 --> 00:11:03.640
What's this? Did you beg
Santa Claus to bring this?

00:11:06.470 --> 00:11:07.640
A coffin?

00:11:09.390 --> 00:11:13.430
Hishigata, you succeeded 
in affixing the soul?

00:11:15.440 --> 00:11:17.030
That's the boy from earlier!

00:11:26.870 --> 00:11:30.040
Pyrokinesis? Is there someone inside there?

00:11:33.790 --> 00:11:38.920
Hmph, well deflected, vermin.
But what about <i>this</i> one?

00:11:38.920 --> 00:11:44.180
Your kind, who only use your
abilities for yourselves, are evil!

00:11:44.180 --> 00:11:45.550
You can't protect anything!

00:11:45.550 --> 00:11:47.470
You can't save anyone!

00:11:47.470 --> 00:11:52.190
Evil is to be chewed up
by the fangs of justice!

00:11:53.520 --> 00:11:55.810
I can't save anyone?

00:12:12.250 --> 00:12:15.380
You really like playing
at being a force for right?

00:12:15.380 --> 00:12:22.180
Then go ahead and try chewing up
the evil that I am, standing before you!

00:12:23.300 --> 00:12:28.780
And if you can't, go ahead
and bite into your own arms!

00:12:30.220 --> 00:12:33.060
It's all the same flavor anyway,

00:12:33.190 --> 00:12:39.020
though compared to me,
yours is a whole lot weaker!

00:12:39.900 --> 00:12:44.410
Screw that! Don't you compare us
to a villain like yourself!

00:12:44.610 --> 00:12:46.320
Limiter released!

00:13:04.170 --> 00:13:05.270
Incredible.

00:13:05.800 --> 00:13:08.470
I realize this is your prize toy,

00:13:08.720 --> 00:13:12.220
but it's time to turn it into scrap!

00:13:41.500 --> 00:13:43.720
You think you can get away?!

00:14:04.230 --> 00:14:09.170
What's the meaning of this--sticking
a dead body inside there?

00:14:13.830 --> 00:14:15.790
It's necromancy, all right.

00:14:28.470 --> 00:14:29.510
Don't move.

00:14:29.680 --> 00:14:34.180
Hold on, hold on. Appearances to
the contrary, he's probably a victim.

00:14:34.180 --> 00:14:35.320
Huh?

00:14:36.020 --> 00:14:39.650
Yo. You've had a rough 
time of it, Accelerator.

00:14:39.940 --> 00:14:41.860
Have we met somewhere before?

00:14:41.860 --> 00:14:42.900
Now that's mean.

00:14:43.690 --> 00:14:45.310
We just saw each other yesterday.

00:14:48.110 --> 00:14:49.530
What happened here?

00:14:49.530 --> 00:14:54.280
If you don't know, then you
really weren't involved in this.

00:14:54.280 --> 00:14:55.540
What are you talking about?

00:14:56.080 --> 00:14:58.540
You've got some counterfeits roaming around.

00:14:58.870 --> 00:14:59.790
Huh?

00:15:02.210 --> 00:15:05.460
DA? Never heard of them before.

00:15:05.920 --> 00:15:07.600
And what's with the body?

00:15:08.090 --> 00:15:12.800
She was inside that pile of junk.
She's been dead for two days.

00:15:12.800 --> 00:15:14.640
Huh? What's going on?

00:15:14.890 --> 00:15:18.140
Her vectors are all different
from somebody alive.

00:15:18.140 --> 00:15:22.650
She's been preserved, and looks clean enough,
but she's not freshly dead.

00:15:23.060 --> 00:15:27.070
He's right. This body belongs
to Hitokawa Hasami.

00:15:27.820 --> 00:15:29.650
1st-year at Ninoude High School.

00:15:29.650 --> 00:15:32.280
She committed suicide by jumping
into a river three days ago,

00:15:32.280 --> 00:15:34.780
and she was pronounced dead
during transport by the rescue team.

00:15:34.990 --> 00:15:39.410
But you said the robot was
using esper abilities, didn't you?

00:15:39.410 --> 00:15:44.080
The guys posing as you stole the body,
stuffed it inside this junk,

00:15:44.080 --> 00:15:47.420
and must have drawn
her ability out of her dead brain.

00:15:47.420 --> 00:15:51.090
Assuming that's all true, she's a Level 2.

00:15:51.090 --> 00:15:55.720
Any way you look at it, it would
take a Level 4 to create a scene like this.

00:15:55.850 --> 00:16:00.350
Heh, so they didn't just draw it out,
they raised its level, too.

00:16:00.350 --> 00:16:02.600
I've never heard of that happening before.

00:16:02.770 --> 00:16:04.440
What does it mean?

00:16:04.560 --> 00:16:08.260
It's <i>your</i> job to look into that, isn't it?

00:16:11.320 --> 00:16:13.610
Did you come into contact with the patients?

00:16:13.610 --> 00:16:16.330
Contact with the patients was prohibited.

00:16:16.780 --> 00:16:20.200
The way things played out, it was unavoidable.
But more importantly,

00:16:20.200 --> 00:16:22.960
that coffin was all but useless!

00:16:23.170 --> 00:16:25.920
We can't fight against 
espers with those things!

00:16:26.170 --> 00:16:29.380
Yeah, I don't know what to tell you.

00:16:29.760 --> 00:16:34.010
I did warn you that it was
just an experimental prototype.

00:16:34.010 --> 00:16:37.350
<i>You're</i> the one who insisted
on taking it with you, right?

00:16:37.680 --> 00:16:41.810
But you said the thing had
Level 4-class power, didn't you?!

00:16:42.140 --> 00:16:47.480
That's right. Mm-hmm, the boost
is based on the level of the subject.

00:16:47.480 --> 00:16:51.280
What you saw was the result of
the ability being elevated that much.

00:16:51.280 --> 00:16:56.280
For that to get beaten must mean that
you got pretty unlucky, or, mm-hmm,

00:16:56.280 --> 00:16:59.620
you were taking on a Level 5-class opponent.

00:16:59.620 --> 00:17:01.040
A certain someone who proposed

00:17:01.040 --> 00:17:03.850
that you not come into contact
with the patients would probably know.

00:17:05.000 --> 00:17:10.710
Oh, now, it doesn't really matter, does it?
We did secure the objective.

00:17:10.710 --> 00:17:14.300
First order of business is to
get her delivered to Dachshund.

00:17:14.300 --> 00:17:18.890
Without her, we can't move the
Waste Recycle Experiment to the next step.

00:17:18.890 --> 00:17:20.930
Mm-hmm, that's right.

00:17:21.890 --> 00:17:24.100
What's the matter? Hurry 
and get her over here.

00:17:24.480 --> 00:17:28.360
The thing is, while we <i>did</i> have
her in custody, she got away.

00:17:28.730 --> 00:17:30.190
Huh? Seriously?

00:17:30.190 --> 00:17:33.900
Nobody could have anticipated
what happened! This isn't on me!

00:17:34.110 --> 00:17:35.570
No, it <i>is</i>.

00:17:35.570 --> 00:17:39.620
You clearly failed.
My client will be disappointed.

00:17:39.620 --> 00:17:43.120
Justice that cannot
correct evil has no value to us.

00:17:43.120 --> 00:17:45.830
DA is supposed to be an organization

00:17:45.830 --> 00:17:49.170
that brings about perfect justice
in Academy City, isn't it?

00:17:49.340 --> 00:17:52.420
I have no intention of
keeping dogs that are all bark.

00:17:52.420 --> 00:17:53.630
W-Wait!

00:17:54.170 --> 00:17:58.010
Dachshund, can we leave
this up to you to deal with?

00:17:58.010 --> 00:18:00.390
Yeah, I guess. Mm-hmm.

00:18:00.390 --> 00:18:01.890
All right.

00:18:01.890 --> 00:18:04.040
The Qiong Qi alone should get it done, right?

00:18:07.140 --> 00:18:10.650
W-Wait a minute.
I can still bring about justice.

00:18:10.650 --> 00:18:14.860
Nah. Your body is useless to me,
so maybe I'll dissolve you.

00:18:15.610 --> 00:18:23.090
D-Don't... Stay away...
Stay away! Stop! Stay away!

00:18:35.920 --> 00:18:36.760
"Hold on...

00:18:39.390 --> 00:18:41.350
Where have you been?"

00:18:41.350 --> 00:18:45.600
asks Misaka Misaka, worrying
about you having a night life...

00:18:45.810 --> 00:18:48.390
I just went to buy a can of coffee.

00:18:48.390 --> 00:18:52.060
"I told you, you shouldn't
drink coffee at this hour,"

00:18:52.060 --> 00:18:55.110
says Misaka Misaka,
concerned about your health...

00:18:55.730 --> 00:18:58.820
Little kids shouldn't be awake at this hour.

00:18:58.820 --> 00:19:00.820
Hurry on back to your room and go to sleep.

00:19:00.820 --> 00:19:04.370
"Hmm, you shouldn't talk to me like that,"

00:19:04.370 --> 00:19:06.520
says Misaka Misaka...

00:19:07.410 --> 00:19:08.040
Tch!

00:19:08.620 --> 00:19:13.290
"What?" asks Misaka Misaka,
regarding your attitude suspiciously.

00:19:16.920 --> 00:19:19.840
You're not going anywhere, right?

00:19:20.090 --> 00:19:23.860
Huh? What are you talking about?

00:19:24.970 --> 00:19:27.730
No, I'm not going anywhere.

00:19:28.810 --> 00:19:30.190
Now, go back to bed.

00:19:34.020 --> 00:19:34.860
Mm-hmm.

00:19:42.780 --> 00:19:43.990
Huh?

00:19:46.410 --> 00:19:47.450
You...

00:19:48.330 --> 00:19:51.170
My name is Esther Rosenthal.

00:19:52.210 --> 00:19:54.630
Thank you for saving me.

00:19:55.500 --> 00:20:00.970
I need a favor. It may sound brazen,
after you already saved me once,

00:20:00.970 --> 00:20:04.220
but I can't stand against them all by myself.

00:20:04.220 --> 00:20:05.490
I need your help--

00:20:06.060 --> 00:20:10.350
Don't get the wrong idea.
I'm no champion of justice.

00:20:10.350 --> 00:20:13.190
For you to intentionally come back in here,

00:20:13.190 --> 00:20:16.190
the inside of your head
must be a pretty happy place.

00:20:16.320 --> 00:20:19.440
No, you aren't a bad person.

00:20:19.440 --> 00:20:20.860
Huh?

00:20:20.860 --> 00:20:25.180
From the look in your eyes when that
body came out of the coffin prototype...

00:20:26.240 --> 00:20:28.660
Those weren't the eyes of a bad person.

00:20:28.830 --> 00:20:31.460
That's quite the entertaining 
story, isn't it?

00:20:31.460 --> 00:20:36.630
Here, let me prove how bad
a person I am by wringing your neck.

00:20:38.460 --> 00:20:40.420
Then so be it!

00:20:40.760 --> 00:20:41.680
Huh?

00:20:42.300 --> 00:20:46.300
But in return, please do
something with your power!

00:20:46.300 --> 00:20:50.770
The way things are headed,
this city--no, the whole world is at risk!

00:20:50.770 --> 00:20:54.730
That body--the reason she
ended up like that is because of me.

00:20:54.730 --> 00:20:59.020
I was the one who taught them
how to control dead bodies like that.

00:20:59.190 --> 00:21:03.530
It's because of me that so many
more people are going to die.

00:21:03.530 --> 00:21:06.240
I was trying to salvage this by myself.

00:21:06.240 --> 00:21:10.950
They're trying to use Last Order
and shift the world into a new level.

00:21:10.950 --> 00:21:15.460
After you tear me to pieces,
make sure you do something about it!

00:21:15.460 --> 00:21:16.500
Please!

00:21:21.760 --> 00:21:25.930
I tell you I'm a bad person,
and you decide to dump your work on me?

00:21:25.930 --> 00:21:27.140
What are you, touched in the head?

00:21:27.640 --> 00:21:30.860
How rude. I'm right as rain.

00:21:30.860 --> 00:21:33.140
Tell me where they are.

00:21:33.140 --> 00:21:33.890
Huh?

00:21:34.390 --> 00:21:37.190
The location of those phony Antiskill guys.

00:21:37.190 --> 00:21:41.860
Whatever it is they're after,
all I have to do is go there and smash it.

00:21:42.280 --> 00:21:47.070
A-All I know is the warehouse
where they kept me locked up.

00:21:47.070 --> 00:21:50.030
I think it's just one of
several hideouts they have.

00:21:50.030 --> 00:21:51.240
Lead the way.

00:21:51.240 --> 00:21:52.320
R-Right.

00:21:54.710 --> 00:21:57.540
You say I don't look like a bad person?

00:21:58.040 --> 00:22:00.000
No. You don't.

00:22:00.290 --> 00:22:04.800
Hmph. I'll show you the style of a villain.

00:23:34.970 --> 00:23:36.960
"Next time"

00:23:36.960 --> 00:23:42.150
"Numbers"
